JB-2.03a — the eyedropper's cancel rule, for the owner of JbCanvasView.kt to apply.

Written by the JB-2.03a audit-fix pass, which does not edit this file (LEAD_DESK rule 3, ROADMAP R30
item 2). It applies to the tree as it stands after the branch bunny/JB-2.03a-audit-fixes, i.e. it needs
Eyedropper.armsCancel / Eyedropper.overCancel / Eyedropper.cancelRadiusPx to exist (they are in the same
branch, in androidkit/tools/Eyedropper.kt). Apply with:

    git apply tasks/joybrush/held/JbCanvasView_JB-2.03a-audit.patch

WHAT IS WRONG, in one paragraph. A long-press eyedropper takes NOTHING if the pen lifts without first
moving 12 dp. startEyedrop puts the cancel circle on the touch point and eyedropMove puts the finger on
that same point, so the touch is inside the circle from the instant the ring appears; eyedropEnd computes
took = take && !overCancel, so the spec's own check "long-press again and lift → red" cannot pass. The
circle is a way BACK to where the hold began, and a touch that has never left it has nothing to go back
from, so the circle is not a cancel until it has been outside once. That second piece of state is what
hunks 2, 4, 5 and 6 add.

THE SEVEN HUNKS. 1 and 7: a second stroke-ended signal, onStrokeCommitted, which fires only for a stroke
that was committed — the recent-colours bar's rule (D.02c Decision 3) and nothing else; the push moves in
the Activity patch. 2, 4, 5, 6: the cancel rule. 3: the lift's own point reaches overCancel(), so a slide
back into the circle that happens inside one frame is still a cancel. 3 is not in the audit's list; I
found it while verifying the rest, and it is the one hunk I would not drop.

THE EVIDENCE, since none of this can be run off-device: EyedropperTest.aHoldThatLiftsWhereItBeganTakesTheColour
and EyedropperTest.slidingBackToTheStartCircleAfterLeavingItCancels pin the rule the hunks call. They go
red if `armed &&` is dropped from Eyedropper.overCancel, if the `!insideCircle` is dropped from
Eyedropper.armsCancel, or if insideCircle's boundary changes from <= to <. They do NOT prove the view
calls them — that is the owner's check on the Note 9: long-press, ring appears, lift without moving → the
colour is taken; long-press, slide 13 dp out, slide back, lift → unchanged.

